('L2.2', 'leader', 'Write a grant proposal', 'I am a principal of a low-income middle school. I want to create a makerspace in our school where students can use AI and other technologies to engage in creative problem-solving. Write a grant proposal to a local foundation that requests funding for the makerspace. The proposal should include a description of the project, a budget, and a plan for how the makerspace will be used to support student learning and creativity.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L2.2', 'sped', 'Design an accessible coding curriculum', 'I am a special education teacher who works with high school students with visual impairments. I want to teach my students how to code, but most coding platforms are not accessible. Design a 10-week coding curriculum that is fully accessible to students who are blind or have low vision. The curriculum should use a combination of text-based and audio-based coding tools, and it should include a variety of engaging projects that allow students to be creative.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L2.2', 'sped', 'Create a social story about AI', 'I am a speech-language pathologist. I work with a [grade level] student with autism who is anxious about using a new AI-powered reading tutor. Create a social story that explains what the AI tutor is, how it works, and how it can help the student become a better reader. The story should be written in simple language and include pictures to support comprehension.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L2.2', 'support', 'Develop a digital citizenship curriculum', 'I am a school librarian. I have been asked to develop a new digital citizenship curriculum for our K-5 students. The curriculum should address the ethical and responsible use of AI, as well as other topics such as online safety, media literacy, and cyberbullying. Generate a curriculum map that outlines the key topics to be covered in each grade level, as well as a list of recommended resources and activities.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L2.2', 'support', 'Create a parent workshop on AI', 'I am a technology integration specialist. I am hosting a workshop for parents on the topic of AI and education. Create a presentation for the workshop that explains what AI is, how it is being used in our schools, and how parents can support their children''s learning in the age of AI. The presentation should be engaging and informative, and it should include time for questions and discussion.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'classroom', 'Differentiated Study Guides', 'Act as an expert instructional designer. I am teaching a [grade level] unit on ecology. My class has three distinct reading levels: on-grade, below-grade, and advanced. Generate three distinct study guides for the unit. Each guide should cover the key concepts of food webs, biomes, and symbiosis, but be adapted for the designated reading level. For the below-grade group, include a vocabulary list with simple definitions. For the advanced group, include two challenge questions that require synthesis.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'classroom', 'Spaced Repetition Quiz Schedule', 'I need to create a spaced repetition schedule for my [grade level] physics class to help them master the concepts of kinematics. The key topics are displacement, velocity, acceleration, and projectile motion. Generate a 4-week schedule that tells students which topic to review each day, with increasing intervals between reviews of the same topic. For each day, also generate 3 practice problems related to that day''s topic.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'coach', 'Peer Observation Feedback', 'I just observed a teacher attempting to use AI to generate a study plan with their class for the first time. The teacher''s prompt was too vague (''make a study guide''). The AI''s response was generic and not very helpful. Write three supportive, constructive feedback prompts I can use to guide the teacher toward more effective prompting. The feedback should be framed as questions to encourage reflection.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'coach', 'collaborative team Discussion Protocol', 'Design a protocol for a 60-minute Professional Learning Community (collaborative team) meeting focused on analyzing the quality of AI-generated retrieval practice questions. The protocol should guide teachers through the process of selecting a common text, each generating their own questions using AI, and then collectively evaluating the questions based on criteria like clarity, curriculum alignment, and cognitive complexity.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'higher_ed', 'Syllabus Policy on AI', 'Draft a syllabus policy on the use of AI tools for my undergraduate ''Foundations of Education'' course. The policy should permit the use of AI for brainstorming and generating study aids but prohibit its use for writing final submitted essays. Provide clear examples of acceptable and unacceptable use, and explain the pedagogical rationale for the policy.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'higher_ed', 'Analyze Student-AI Interactions', 'I have a dataset of transcripts from pre-service professionals using an AI chatbot to practice their questioning skills. Act as a qualitative researcher. Analyze the attached transcripts and identify common patterns in how the program candidates are using the AI. Are they asking low-level or high-level questions? Are they effectively rephrasing questions when the AI gives a basic response? Summarize your findings in a short report.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'leader', 'PD Feedback Analysis', 'I have collected 50 anonymous feedback responses from teachers after a professional development session on AI for retrieval practice. The responses are in a spreadsheet. Act as a data analyst. Identify the top 3 themes of what teachers found most valuable and the top 3 areas where they still need support. Summarize the findings in a bulleted list I can share with my instructional leadership team.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'leader', 'AI Tool Vetting Rubric', 'Our district is considering adopting a new AI-powered tool for creating study materials. Create a rubric for evaluating such tools. The rubric should include criteria such as curriculum alignment, ease of use for teachers and students, data privacy and security, and the quality of the generated content (e.g., accuracy, bias). The rubric should use a 4-point scale from ''Does Not Meet'' to ''Exceeds Expectations''.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'sped', 'Text-to-Audio Study Guide', 'I have a [grade level] student with dyslexia who needs to learn about the branches of the U.S. government. Take the provided text on this topic and convert it into a simple study guide. Then, for each section of the guide, generate a script for a text-to-audio tool that reads the content in a clear, slow-paced voice. The script should include pauses for processing.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'sped', 'Social Story for Study Skills', 'Create a short social story for a student with autism spectrum disorder about how to use an AI tool to study for a test. The story should be written in the first person and describe the steps of breaking down a big topic, asking the AI for practice questions, and what to do if they get a question wrong. Use simple language and a reassuring tone.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'support', 'Bilingual Study Aid', 'I am supporting a group of newcomer English Language Learners in [grade level] biology. They are learning about cell structures. Create a bilingual study guide in English and Spanish. The guide should list 10 key vocabulary terms (e.g., ''nucleus,'' ''mitochondria'') with a simple definition and a supporting image for each term. Provide the English and Spanish terms side-by-side.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.1', 'support', 'Study Hall ''Quiz Bowl''', 'Generate a ''Quiz Bowl'' game for a mixed-grade-level study hall (grades 6-8). The game should have 20 questions covering a range of middle school subjects: 5 math, 5 science, 5 history, and 5 literature questions. The questions should be fun and engaging, designed for teams to answer collaboratively.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'classroom', 'Multi-day Reflection Arc', 'I am teaching a 3-day mini-unit on the water cycle to my [grade level]rs. Generate a sequence of three daily reflection prompts. The first should activate prior knowledge, the second should focus on the process of a hands-on activity, and the third should ask students to synthesize their learning and apply it to a real-world scenario.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'classroom', 'Analyze and Group Student Reflections', 'I have a set of 25 student reflections on the question: ''What was the most challenging part of the research project for you?'' Read all 25 reflections, identify the 3-4 most common challenges cited by students, and provide a percentage breakdown of how many students mentioned each challenge.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'coach', 'Differentiated Coaching Plan', 'I support three [grade level] [subject area] teachers with varying levels of tech integration skills. Based on their self-assessments (pasted below), generate a differentiated coaching plan for helping each of them incorporate AI into their practice for student reflection. Suggest a specific, manageable first step for each teacher.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'coach', 'Connecting Reflection to Observation Data', 'I just completed a classroom observation where I noted that students seemed disengaged during the lesson''s closing activity. The teacher wants to improve this. Generate three different AI-powered reflection activities the teacher could use as a lesson closure that would also provide them with data on student understanding and engagement.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'higher_ed', 'Critique of AI in Education Research', 'Find and summarize three recent (last 2 years) academic papers on the use of AI for student metacognition or reflection in K-12 settings. For each paper, provide a one-sentence critique of its methodology or conclusions, and suggest one unanswered question for future research.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'higher_ed', 'AI Tool Evaluation Framework', 'Develop a comprehensive evaluation framework for pre-service professionals to use when assessing AI-powered educational tools. The framework should include criteria related to pedagogical soundness, ethical considerations (bias, privacy), usability, and accessibility for diverse learners. Present it as a checklist with guiding questions for each criterion.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'leader', 'Cross-Reference Policy and Practice', 'Given our district''s AI ethics policy (pasted below), analyze the following three teacher-proposed AI projects. For each project, identify potential areas of misalignment with the policy and suggest specific modifications to ensure compliance and ethical integrity. [Paste policy and project descriptions here].', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'leader', 'Strategic Planning from Synthesis', 'I''ve pasted the AI-synthesized notes from our last three leadership team meetings about our school-wide metacognition goal. Based on this data, identify three strategic priorities for the next quarter. For each priority, define a key performance indicator (KPI) and suggest a lead person from the team.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'sped', 'Dynamic Prompt Scaffolding', 'Create a reflection prompt for a [grade level] student with executive function challenges about a long-term project. The prompt should be a checklist that breaks down the reflection into smaller parts: 1. Rate your time management on a scale of 1-5. 2. Identify one thing you did well. 3. Identify one thing you would do differently next time. 4. Choose one strategy to try for the next project (e.g., using a planner, breaking down tasks).', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'sped', 'Multi-modal Journal Analysis', 'A non-verbal student has been keeping a learning journal using a combination of drawings, photos of their work, and short audio recordings. Analyze the past two weeks of entries (I will provide descriptions) and generate a summary for their IEP team about their engagement and perceived areas of confidence and struggle.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'support', 'Proactive Support Identification', 'Analyze the attendance and grade data for all [grade level]rs over the past four weeks (pasted below). Cross-reference this with the list of students who have not submitted their last two learning journal reflections. Identify a list of students who may be at risk and in need of a proactive check-in from a counselor.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.2', 'support', 'Thematic Analysis of Counseling Notes', 'I have anonymized notes from my last 15 counseling sessions with high school students. Identify the most common recurring themes related to academic anxiety. Based on these themes, what are two metacognitive strategies I could introduce in a small group counseling session to address these anxieties?', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'classroom', 'Create Differentiated Learning Paths', 'Act as an expert instructional designer. I have a [grade level] [subject area] class with diverse learning needs. Based on their pre-assessment data for our unit on ecosystems (data attached), create three distinct learning paths: one for students who need foundational review, one for students at grade level, and one for students ready for enrichment. For each path, suggest a key learning activity, a resource, and a brief mastery check.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'classroom', 'Develop a Mastery-Based Rubric', 'I need a mastery-based rubric for a [grade level] [subject area] argumentative essay assignment. The rubric should have four levels: Beginning, Developing, Proficient, and Exemplary. Create criteria for the following three standards: Strength of Claim, Use of Evidence, and Organization. For each standard and performance level, write a clear, student-friendly descriptor.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'coach', 'Generate a Playlist of Differentiated Coaching Strategies', 'Act as an expert instructional coach. I support teachers with a wide range of experience and comfort levels with technology. Create a ''playlist'' of coaching strategies I can use to help teachers integrate AI for mastery tracking. The playlist should include options for ''getting started'' (e.g., co-planning with an AI assistant), ''going deeper'' (e.g., analyzing AI-generated data), and ''innovating'' (e.g., designing an AI-powered project).', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'coach', 'Script a Difficult Coaching Conversation', 'I need to have a difficult conversation with a teacher who is resistant to using data and technology to inform their instruction. The teacher values their autonomy and experience. Act as a veteran instructional coach and script the key talking points for this conversation. The script should be empathetic, asset-based, and focused on student learning rather than compliance.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'higher_ed', 'Design a University-School Partnership for AI Integration', 'Act as a university professor of educational technology. Propose a detailed plan for a partnership between our School of Education and a local K-12 school district to support the ethical and effective integration of AI for mastery learning. The plan should outline joint research projects, professional development opportunities for in-service teachers, and practicum experiences for students in your program.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'higher_ed', 'Generate a Policy Brief on AI and Academic Rigor', 'Write a policy brief for state-level education policymakers on the topic of ''Maintaining Academic Rigor in the Age of AI.'' The brief should define academic rigor in an AI context, identify the potential risks AI poses to rigor (e.g., over-simplification of tasks), and provide three concrete policy recommendations to help schools leverage AI to increase, rather than decrease, academic challenge.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'leader', 'Generate a Data-Driven School Improvement Plan', 'Act as a data analyst for a K-8 school. I am providing you with three years of anonymized state assessment data in math and ELA, as well as student attendance and discipline data. Analyze this data to identify two key trends and propose three strategic, evidence-based goals for our School Improvement Plan for the upcoming year. For each goal, suggest a key initiative and a metric for success.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'leader', 'Create a Communication Plan for a New AI Initiative', 'Our district is rolling out a new AI-powered platform for tracking student mastery and providing personalized learning recommendations. Act as a communications director and create a comprehensive communication plan for this initiative. The plan should include key messages, target audiences (teachers, students, parents, school board), communication channels, and a timeline for the first three months.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'sped', 'Design an Adaptive Learning Intervention', 'Act as a special education technology specialist. I have a student with a specific learning disability in reading comprehension who is working on making inferences. Design a 4-week adaptive learning intervention plan using AI. The plan should start with highly structured tasks and gradually release responsibility to the student, incorporating AI tools that can provide instant feedback and scaffolded support.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'sped', 'Automate IEP Goal Tracking', 'I need to track progress for multiple students on their IEP goals. Create a template for a prompt that I can use weekly. The prompt should allow me to input a student''s specific IEP goal, my observational notes, and a piece of student work, and then ask the AI to summarize the current progress level, calculate the new percentage of mastery, and suggest a next instructional step.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'support', 'Develop a Tiered Intervention Menu', 'Act as a Multi-Tiered System of Supports (MTSS) coordinator. Based on the principles of MTSS, create a tiered menu of academic interventions for a middle school. For each tier (Tier 1, Tier 2, Tier 3), provide three evidence-based intervention strategies for reading and three for math. Specify the recommended frequency, duration, and progress monitoring tool for each strategy.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('L3.3', 'support', 'Create a Student Success Plan Template', 'I am a school counselor working with students who are at risk of not graduating. Create a comprehensive Student Success Plan template. The template should be a collaborative document for the student, counselor, and family, and include sections for: student strengths and interests, academic goals, attendance goals, post-secondary aspirations, and a checklist of action steps with assigned responsibilities.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'classroom', 'Create a Rubric', 'Act as a [grade level] [subject area] teacher. Create a rubric to evaluate a student-created podcast episode about the causes of the American Revolution. The rubric should include criteria for historical accuracy, narrative structure, audio quality, and the ethical use of AI-generated content or voice cloning. Ensure the rubric is written in student-friendly language.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'classroom', 'Design a Learning Station', 'I''m designing a learning station activity for my [grade level] class on the topic of animal habitats. One station will involve using a generative AI tool. Design a task for this station where students use AI to create a short descriptive paragraph about an animal and its habitat, but they must also verify the AI''s output using a designated non-AI resource (e.g., a specific website or book). Write the student instructions for this station.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'coach', 'Design a Coaching Cycle', 'Act as an instructional coach. Design a 3-week coaching cycle focused on helping a [grade level] [subject area] teacher integrate AI into their algebra class. The plan should include a pre-observation meeting, an observation focus, and a post-observation reflection protocol. The goal is to use AI to create personalized practice problems for students.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'coach', 'Curate AI Prompts for Inquiry', 'I am an instructional coach supporting a team of [grade level] teachers who are planning a project-based learning unit on environmental conservation. Curate a list of 10 generative AI prompts that students could use at various stages of the inquiry process (e.g., generating research questions, summarizing articles, creating an advocacy campaign). The prompts should encourage critical thinking, not just information retrieval.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'higher_ed', 'Develop an Ethics Case Study', 'Act as a professor of education. Develop a detailed case study for a university course about a scenario where a student observes their mentor using an AI-powered grading tool that shows clear evidence of bias against students who are English language learners. The case study should end with a series of discussion questions that prompt preservice teachers to consider the ethical, pedagogical, and professional implications.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'higher_ed', 'Write a Grant Proposal Snippet', 'I am writing a grant proposal to fund a study on the use of AI for teacher professional development. Write a compelling 250-word "Needs Assessment" section for this proposal. Use recent statistics and research findings to argue that K-12 teachers urgently need more effective and scalable training on how to use AI responsibly and effectively in their classrooms.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'leader', 'Analyze Survey Data', 'Act as a school principal. I have just surveyed my staff about their attitudes and skills regarding AI in education. Here is the raw data: [paste anonymized survey data]. Analyze this data to identify three key trends and recommend three specific action steps I should take to support my staff''s professional growth in this area.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'leader', 'Prepare for a Board Meeting', 'I am a district superintendent preparing for a school board meeting where I will propose the adoption of a new, district-wide AI platform. Generate a list of potential questions and concerns the board members might have. For each question, provide a concise and evidence-based talking point to address it.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'sped', 'Adapt a Science Experiment', 'Act as a special education teacher. I need to adapt a standard [grade level] science experiment on building electrical circuits for a student who has fine motor difficulties and is easily overwhelmed by multi-step directions. Generate a new set of instructions that breaks the experiment down into smaller, more manageable steps, includes visual cues, and suggests ways to use an AI simulation as an alternative or supplement to the hands-on activity.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'sped', 'Create a UDL Lesson Plan', 'Create a lesson plan for a [grade level] [subject area] class on the theme of identity, using the principles of Universal Design for Learning (UDL). The lesson should incorporate generative AI in a way that provides multiple means of engagement, representation, and action/expression. For example, students could use AI to generate a poem, a song, or a visual representation of their identity.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'support', 'Automate Attendance Emails', 'Act as a school secretary. I need to send daily attendance emails to parents of absent students. Create a template for this email that can be easily automated. The template should include a placeholder for the student''s name, the date, and a link to the school''s attendance policy. Also, write a brief, friendly reminder about the importance of regular school attendance.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.1', 'support', 'Create a Tech Support Guide', 'Act as a school technology specialist. A common issue students are facing is how to properly cite generative AI as a source in their schoolwork. Create a simple, one-page guide with examples of how to cite ChatGPT, Gemini, and Claude in both MLA and APA formats. The guide should be written for a middle school audience.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.2', 'classroom', 'Design a Project-Based Learning Unit on AI Ethics', 'Design a project-based learning unit for your students on the topic of AI ethics. The unit should culminate in a student-led project that addresses a real-world problem related to AI and bias.', 0, NOW(), NOW()),
('T1.2', 'classroom', 'Create a Student-Led AI Ethics Committee', 'Develop a proposal for a student-led AI ethics committee at your school. The proposal should outline the committee''s mission, goals, and activities.', 1, NOW(), NOW()),
